{
  "slug": "molokai-landfill-limits-for-hazardous-and-disaster-debris",
  "title": "Molokaʻi landfill limits for hazardous and disaster debris",
  "summary": "At the December 11 meeting, a landfill official said debris from even a medium-sized disaster probably would not fit in the landfill, whose life estimate uses average yearly tons, and that it cannot take hazardous waste but can take some special waste. The official said he could probably get past tonnage data and the annual report. In October the commission unanimously denied the exemption, so the project would return as an Special Management Area (SMA) minor permit.",
